cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ICE: Infinite Context Engine (v2-paper-eval)"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Deepesh
    family-names: Sonar
    email: 18deepnar@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1762-4246"
    affiliation: "Thakur College of Engineering and Technology, Mumbai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Deepnar/ice"
abstract: >-
  Frozen ICE v2 is a local-first conversational memory middleware with typed
  stores, retrieval fusion, and dynamic context budgets. The accompanying
  LSREP paper reports 52 checkpoints and 1,211 observations of 219 distinct
  probes from four private conversations. Mechanism-fidelity and matched
  LongMemEval analyses bound the measured capabilities; several defined paths
  were defective or unexercised, and graph utility is unconfirmed. This software
  citation identifies the frozen evaluation version, not current ICE v3.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - long-term memory
  - large language models
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - knowledge graphs
  - evaluation methodology
  - local-first
license: Apache-2.0
version: v2-paper-eval
date-released: "2026-08-01"
